# Jira ticket flow (no confirmation prompts)

When the user's message contains a Jira ticket (a `.../browse/ABC-123` URL or a key like `SCRUM-5`) and asks for tests or automation, or gives the ticket on its own, run every step below in order. Do **not** ask for permission for branch creation, `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, or the Jira update. Only stop to ask if a step fails in a way you cannot fix.

1. **Branch**: `git fetch origin`, then `git checkout -b <KEY_with_underscore>_<short_summary_slug> origin/main` (example: `SCRUM_5_contractual_job_search`). If that branch exists, check it out instead.
2. **Fetch + analyse**: fetch the ticket per `.cursor/skills/jira-xray-testcase/SKILL.md` (base URL from `.env`; add `https://` if missing). Analyse it per `.cursor/skills/requirement-analysis/SKILL.md`.
3. **Test cases**: write `generated_test_cases/<KEY>.csv` (Xray format) per the jira-xray-testcase and testcase-generation skills. Always include positive, negative, and boundary cases.
4. **Locators + automation**: inspect the live page for locators (`.cursor/skills/locator-review/SKILL.md`), then write `tests/<Feature>_<KEY>.spec.ts` per `.cursor/skills/playwright-automation/SKILL.md`, reusing page objects. Tag the first test `['@smoke', '@regression']` and every other test `'@regression'`.
5. **Review**: self-review the new code per `.cursor/skills/code-review/SKILL.md` and fix issues found.
6. **Run**: clear old Allure results (`npm run allure:clean`), then `npx playwright test tests/<Feature>_<KEY>.spec.ts --reporter=line,allure-playwright` (a bare `--reporter=line` replaces the config reporters and leaves `allure-results` empty). Fix test-code problems and re-run; do not weaken assertions to hide real app bugs.
7. **Jira update** (only if all tests pass): `npm run jira:after-automation -- <KEY>`. This writes the test cases and steps into the ticket description and moves it To Do -> In Review. If tests fail, skip this and report the failures.
8. **Git**: `git add` only the files for this ticket (never `.env`, `screenshots/`, reports), commit with message `Add <KEY> <summary> test cases and automation.`, and `git push -u origin <branch>`.
9. **Pull request**: if `gh` is available, `gh pr create --base main --fill`. Otherwise give the user a pre-filled `https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/compare/main...<branch>?expand=1&title=...&body=...` link.
10. **Report**: summarise per `.cursor/skills/reporting/SKILL.md`, then run `npm run allure:generate` and open it with `npm run allure:open` (in the background, since it keeps a server running).

If `.env` is missing or Jira returns 401/404, run `npm run doctor`, show the user its Jira line, and ask them to fill in their own `JIRA_EMAIL` / `JIRA_API_TOKEN` (see `.env.example`).

Never print or commit the Jira API token.
